WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.200
-Jack Whitehall!
-Hi!

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.033
-It is great to see you
and back in the studio.

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:06.467
-Back in the studio, back in
New York, this is amazing.

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:07.501
-Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:07.501 --> 00:00:08.834
I appreciate it, bud.

00:00:08.834 --> 00:00:10.100
I want to first of all
congratulate you

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:11.267
on "Jungle Cruise."

00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:13.234
It was the biggest hit
of the summer.

00:00:13.234 --> 00:00:15.334
So congratulations.
-Oh, thank you very much.

00:00:15.334 --> 00:00:17.234
-I heard they're making
a sequel.

00:00:17.234 --> 00:00:20.400
-Yes. I think the sequel is
in development now.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.033
I absolutely loved
making that movie.

00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:23.133
It was so much fun.

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:25.934
Dwayne and Emily Blunt
are incredible.

00:00:25.934 --> 00:00:27.701
-Did you ever work out
with The Rock?

00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:30.267
-I did once, yes. Can you tell?

00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:31.634
-Yes. That's why I was asking.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.634 --> 00:00:33.200
That's what I was asking.
-Physical transformation.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.834
A lot of people ask me that
when they see me.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.501
They're like, "This guy must
spot The Rock."

00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:38.834
-Yeah.
-"He's built."

00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:42.467
As he had obviously seen me
and realized that

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:46.234
Dwayne and I have slightly
different physiques --

00:00:46.234 --> 00:00:50.334
you know, he is obviously
quite generously proportioned,

00:00:50.334 --> 00:00:53.200
and I have a body that looks
like it's been drawn by a child.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:54.634
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:58.400
So before I arrived at the gym,
he had gone round to all

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.934
of the machines and he had
taken all of the weights

00:01:00.934 --> 00:01:03.100
off the machines
so it was just the bars.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:04.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.767 --> 00:01:08.434
But as you know, like, even
those bars are pretty heavy.

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:10.801
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, come on.

00:01:10.801 --> 00:01:12.968
-No, 'cause that's my worst
nightmare, being in there, like,

00:01:12.968 --> 00:01:16.267
trapped underneath a bar
in front of one of your heroes.

00:01:16.267 --> 00:01:17.834
So I was like, "Do you know
what? I think I'm just going to

00:01:17.834 --> 00:01:20.801
take the exercise bike in the
corner. That one's good for me."

00:01:20.801 --> 00:01:22.534
So it was so surreal.

00:01:22.534 --> 00:01:24.434
Like, he's down one end
of the gym,

00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:26.667
like, eating dumbbells
for breakfast.

00:01:26.667 --> 00:01:29.334
Chain round his neck,
listening to gangster rap.

00:01:29.334 --> 00:01:32.000
And then I was in the other
corner just trundling along

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.200
on an exercise bike,
listening to an audiobook.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:36.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:39.667
Yeah. Jane Austen,
"Pride and Prejudice."

00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:41.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:43.701
No Janes, no gains.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.701 --> 00:01:46.767
-You work out to Jane Austen.
-Yeah!

00:01:46.767 --> 00:01:48.334
-I want to ask you about this,
because now you have

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:50.667
"Jungle Cruise," now you have
"Clifford the Big Red Dog."

00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:52.868
You're becoming like
a family superstar,

00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:55.501
like family movies
for Jack Whitehall.

00:01:55.501 --> 00:01:57.300
But do you get excited
when you see a poster

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:59.534
or a trailer
for your new movies?

00:01:59.534 --> 00:02:01.534
-Oh, my God. Amazing.
Yeah, I still have

00:02:01.534 --> 00:02:04.801
imposter syndrome and feel,
like, so lucky to be able

00:02:04.801 --> 00:02:06.801
to be doing what I'm doing.

00:02:06.801 --> 00:02:10.667
And I think what's good is that
my fans, especially in England,

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:14.267
are very good at sort of
keeping me in my place.

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:16.734
And they definitely did
with the "Clifford" movie

00:02:16.734 --> 00:02:19.367
'cause, basically for years
when I was a stand-up,

00:02:19.367 --> 00:02:20.701
I did lots of jokes about how

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:23.367
I was at school with
Robert Pattinson, which is true.

00:02:23.367 --> 00:02:24.667
We went to the same school,

00:02:24.667 --> 00:02:26.934
and I was very jealous of him
for some time

00:02:26.934 --> 00:02:28.934
because our careers
sort of happened in parallel.

00:02:28.934 --> 00:02:31.167
And when he was starring
in the "Twilight" films,

00:02:31.167 --> 00:02:33.934
I was an open-mike comedian
in pubs telling

00:02:33.934 --> 00:02:35.968
[bleep] jokes to 30 people.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.968 --> 00:02:38.801
And my mom always used to
compare the two of us.

00:02:38.801 --> 00:02:41.601
And so I basically just, like,
trash-talked him for five years.

00:02:41.601 --> 00:02:42.868
-Yeah.
-And I was like, you know what?

00:02:42.868 --> 00:02:45.367
I just need to like, let that be
and just not obs--

00:02:45.367 --> 00:02:48.000
not let Robert Pattinson
live in my head rent free.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.567
-Yeah, don't worry about
Robert Pattinson.

00:02:49.567 --> 00:02:51.634
-No, no. Who cares about
Robert Pattinson?

00:02:51.634 --> 00:02:53.300
I know right now
it seems like I care.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:54.901
-We do, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.901 --> 00:02:56.868
We actually all really do, yeah.

00:02:56.868 --> 00:02:59.000
But yes, good for you.
-But I stopped it.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.334
And I stopped talking about him.

00:03:00.334 --> 00:03:03.367
And then I think
he had the last laugh

00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:06.968
because a couple of months ago,
my Twitter just exploded

00:03:06.968 --> 00:03:09.200
with people pointing out
that on the day

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:12.801
that they released the trailer
for Robert Pattinson's "Batman,"

00:03:12.801 --> 00:03:15.901
Paramount Pictures released
a trailer that featured me

00:03:15.901 --> 00:03:18.501
being urinated on by
a 10-foot CGI red dog.

00:03:18.501 --> 00:03:20.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:20.734 --> 00:03:22.434
-See, the world wins.

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:25.200
The world wins eventually, yeah.
-We're both killing it.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:28.501
Batman and the dog man just
doing their thing in Hollywood.

00:03:28.501 --> 00:03:29.868
-Batman and the dog man.

00:03:29.868 --> 00:03:32.601
You were very nice enough
to bring us photos

00:03:32.601 --> 00:03:34.367
of you filming this film.

00:03:34.367 --> 00:03:37.334
And so it is a giant,
big, red dog.

00:03:37.334 --> 00:03:39.100
-Yes.
-So this is...

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:42.033
-Yeah, that's what
we acted opposite.

00:03:42.033 --> 00:03:43.267
I know, it's terrifying.

00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:44.634
-That's not the dog, by the way.

00:03:44.634 --> 00:03:46.934
It's not the final CGI.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.934 --> 00:03:49.467
But this is what? These are --
Are these puppeteers?

00:03:49.467 --> 00:03:52.434
-Yeah. There was two puppeteers
who operated this.

00:03:52.434 --> 00:03:53.801
They switched around as well,

00:03:53.801 --> 00:03:55.767
so no one had to be Clifford's
ass for the whole film.

00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:57.634
[ Laughter ]
So you never knew who was

00:03:57.634 --> 00:03:59.334
going to be in the front
and who was going to be

00:03:59.334 --> 00:04:01.601
in the back each day.

00:04:01.601 --> 00:04:03.701
And, yeah, they were amazing.

00:04:03.701 --> 00:04:05.033
Because we didn't just have this
as well.

00:04:05.033 --> 00:04:06.667
We had other, like,
Clifford body parts

00:04:06.667 --> 00:04:08.634
for some of the close-ups.
That was the weird thing.

00:04:08.634 --> 00:04:11.267
So there was, like, some guys
that operated Clifford's tail.

00:04:11.267 --> 00:04:13.334
Clifford's tongue,
which was like someone's arm,

00:04:13.334 --> 00:04:14.634
in, like, this big rubber prop

00:04:14.634 --> 00:04:17.467
that licked people,
which was very disconcerting.

00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:20.167
The weirdest one was the head,
though, because they had a head

00:04:20.167 --> 00:04:22.667
as well, which they used for
some of the shots.

00:04:22.667 --> 00:04:25.167
And you had to do, like --
The little girl who played

00:04:25.167 --> 00:04:26.934
Emily Elizabeth had this
really emotional scene

00:04:26.934 --> 00:04:29.234
when she's saying goodbye to
Clifford the Big Red Dog,

00:04:29.234 --> 00:04:32.868
and she's acting opposite this
guy from the props department

00:04:32.868 --> 00:04:35.567
with his ass hanging out,
like, bent over holding

00:04:35.567 --> 00:04:38.067
Clifford's severed head
on a pike.

00:04:38.067 --> 00:04:40.434
It was like no wonder she's
in tears. It's terrifying!

00:04:40.434 --> 00:04:42.133
It's like something out of
"Game of Thrones."

00:04:42.133 --> 00:04:44.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.067 --> 00:04:46.400
-It's a fun, fun,
fun family movie.

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:48.367
-Yeah, I've really not made it
sound pretty fun.

00:04:48.367 --> 00:04:49.868
[ Laughter ]
It's a really sweet...

00:04:49.868 --> 00:04:51.634
-That's what goes into
making a movie.

00:04:51.634 --> 00:04:54.133
And she is just --
-She's amazing.

00:04:54.133 --> 00:04:56.300
When you watch the finished
version of that scene,

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:57.601
I was going -- I was going.

00:04:57.601 --> 00:04:59.100
-Yeah, it's emotional.
-Were you? Did you? Did you?

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:00.901
-Yeah, of course I did.
-Of course you did.

00:05:00.901 --> 00:05:02.234
-I'm an emotional guy.
-You're an emotional guy.

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:03.234
We're emotional guys.

00:05:03.234 --> 00:05:04.501
-We are.
-We are.

00:05:04.501 --> 00:05:05.834
-And I don't care about
Robert Pattinson.

00:05:05.834 --> 00:05:07.334
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.334 --> 00:05:09.534
[ Crying ] Neither do I.

00:05:09.534 --> 00:05:11.667
-Do you think --
Does he know I exist?

00:05:11.667 --> 00:05:14.934
-Oh, God, when he wins an Oscar,
I'm just going to just

00:05:14.934 --> 00:05:16.534
hide in a hole
for the rest of my life.

00:05:16.534 --> 00:05:18.067
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.067 --> 00:05:19.367
He is. He's going to win
an Oscar, isn't he?

00:05:19.367 --> 00:05:20.901
-He's going to win an Oscar.
Yeah, of course he is.

00:05:20.901 --> 00:05:22.367
-Maybe I'll win an Oscar
for "Clifford."

00:05:22.367 --> 00:05:23.834
-That's what I'm --
You think so?

00:05:23.834 --> 00:05:25.200
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah. Look, they like it!

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:27.167
Here's the Oscar clip.
Everyone, take a look.

00:05:27.167 --> 00:05:29.934
Jack Whitehall
in "Clifford the Big Red Dog."

00:05:29.934 --> 00:05:31.334
Take a look at this.

00:05:31.334 --> 00:05:32.634
-The dishwasher is right there.

00:05:32.634 --> 00:05:34.901
-Yeah, but the water cutoff
is in the bedroom closet.

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:36.667
-Don't -- Don't come in here.
-No.

00:05:36.667 --> 00:05:38.133
-Why not?

00:05:38.133 --> 00:05:40.934
-It's private.
-It's haunted.

00:05:40.934 --> 00:05:42.234
Um, I can do it, though.

00:05:42.234 --> 00:05:44.067
-Yeah, yeah.
Thanks, Uncle Casey.

00:05:44.067 --> 00:05:45.934
-Just get in there and give it
a little [Clicks tongue]

00:05:45.934 --> 00:05:49.601
So, the, um...
-So, the dishwasher.

00:05:49.601 --> 00:05:54.300
So, it makes, like,
this weird crackling noise.

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:56.000
-No, no! Stop!

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.300
[ Clifford whining ]

00:05:57.300 --> 00:05:58.701
[ Grunts ]

00:05:58.701 --> 00:06:01.000
[ Groans ]

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:02.667
Everything's under control

00:06:02.667 --> 00:06:04.234
Just shutting off the valve!

00:06:04.234 --> 00:06:06.400
Aaaah! Ohh!

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:08.400
-There you go!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:11.000
Remember me at the Oscars.
-I'll thank you in my speech.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:12.634
-Thank you.
Jack Whitehall, everybody.

00:06:12.634 --> 00:06:14.667
"Clifford the Big Red Dog"
is in theaters

00:06:14.667 --> 00:06:16.968
and streaming on Paramount+
tomorrow.

